cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its style catalogue, please cite it as below."
title: "RuWritingStyles: Russian Claude custom styles and an agentic review pipeline for scholarly writing on Sanskrit linguistics"
abstract: >-
  RuWritingStyles is a bilingual resource for scholarly writing on Sanskrit
  linguistics in Russian. It combines (1) a catalogue of Russian-language Claude
  custom-style prompts modelled on the prose method of major philologists
  (Zaliznyak, Tronsky, Mel'cuk, Elizarenkova, Toporov, Lidova and others), and
  (2) a zero-runtime-dependency agentic review pipeline that runs a multi-style
  "Council" over a Markdown manuscript (segment, independent style reviews,
  council deliberation, revision, verification) with deterministic Sanskrit
  quality checks: IAST/Cyrillic transliteration consistency, GOST R 7.0.100-2018
  bibliography formatting, and citation grounding. Review panels are selectable
  by named council (general / sanskrit / indology).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gasūns
    given-names: Mārcis
